  "note": "Chapter 19 (LCM & HCF) runs book pp.644-650 (145 questions total, organised by SSC exam year). Batch 1 drew 33 questions from the first two pages (pp.644-645, Q1-44): one new PYQ (Q19) extended the pre-existing q-hl-lcm-offset qtype; the rest introduced q-hl-common-rem, q-hl-remainder-extra, q-hl-hcf-lcm-relation, q-hl-sum-diff, q-hl-ratio-numbers, q-hl-hcf-container, q-hl-hcf-remainder-diff, q-hl-bells, q-hl-perfect-square, q-hl-never-lcm and q-hl-exact-divide. Q20 was dropped there (its computed meeting time matched no printed option). Batch 2 adds 40 more questions from pp.646-650 (Q45-133 of the remaining range), extending every batch-1 qtype with further PYQs and introducing five new ones: q-hl-count-pairs (how many number-pairs fit a given HCF and sum/product), q-hl-ratio-sum (HCF and LCM linked by a sum and a multiple), q-hl-nearest (nearest multiple of the LCM to a target), q-hl-fraction (HCF/LCM of fractions) and q-hl-algebra (symbolic HCF-LCM identities, including prime-power HCF/LCM). Two questions in this range were dropped: Q118 (a fraction-reconstruction word problem whose printed options were not legible in the scan) and Q130 (HCF of two polynomials, x⁶−1 and x⁴+2x³−2x−1 — solved by hand as x²−1, but left unfiled since polynomial HCF is a different skill from numeric HCF/LCM and deserves its own topic-routing decision). Roughly 60 further questions in this range were reviewed and excluded as near-duplicates of patterns already covered twice over, per the \"keep 2-3 similar, not more\" standard. Q134-146 were not reviewed at all, so the chapter is substantially but not exhaustively covered. A genuine printed answer-key table exists for this chapter (book pp.650-651, covering Q1-146, with Q41-49 illegible in the scan) — the first time one has turned up for Chapters 17-20. It was used as a bonus cross-check for both batches (see verify_ry7300-ch19-lcm-hcf.py's BOOK_KEY): nearly every entry matched, but two batch-1 answers disagree with the printed key — Q23 (HCF(75,45): the book key reads (a) 1 litre, but HCF(75,45) = 15 is unambiguous arithmetic, matching the filed (c) 15 litres) and Q31 (least N such that 2N is divisible by LCM(12,18,21,30)=1260: the book key reads (b) 1260, but the least such N is 1260÷2 = 630, matching the filed (c) 630) — both kept as independently recomputed, since recomputation is the primary check and the book key only a bonus. Q50 was also corrected while cross-checking against this key: the remainder common to 5, 6 and 8 is 3, not 2 as first drafted (120k+2 never divides evenly by 9 for any k; 120k+3 does, at k=2, giving 243 — confirmed by the book key).",
